<title>USA: Compaq plans just-in-time production - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Compaq plans just-in-time production - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp plans to tell customers next week it will make business computers when they are ordered, instead of basing production on forecasts, the Wall Street Journal said on Monday.</p>
<p>The company is also moving to ship some models to customers straight from the factories, in order to reduce reliance on its dealer network, the paper said in its electronic edition.</p>
<p>The paper said Compaq would move in May to start making PCs when the orders came in.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
